    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0658" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 868.001 G 29/10.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reports that the body of the King arrived at the Piraeus yesterday, having been
                    delayed one day on account of fog. There was an impressive procession at Athens,
                    the streets were lined with soldiers, while the houses and sidewalks were
                    crowded with spectators. A short service was held at the cathedral in the
                    presence of the Royal family, the Holy Synod, the Cabinet, Diplomatic Corps and
                    officials.</p>
                <p>Thanks the President for his appointment as special representative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
